From: aleks2 (H38)
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] collection-lib: stb_image without thread-local storage on the console

A switch-arm64 module may not use TLS: the loader provides no TLS blocks and H38 adds none. The only TLS in
Twilit Essentials is stb_image's failure reason, inside collection-lib, which the mod links. For the switch-arm64
toolchain collection_lib is compiled with STBI_NO_THREAD_LOCALS (the reason becomes one global).

That is safe because stb_image has a single, single-threaded user: tex_replacements_apply() is its only caller
(decode, stbi_failure_reason and free are all inside it), it is reached from load_icon_uncached on the game thread,
and neither the library nor the mod starts a thread. tex_replacements_apply() now asserts it: the first caller is
taken as the owner thread, and a call from any other is refused (falls back to the original texture) instead of
racing on the decoder.
---
diff --git a/collection-lib/CMakeLists.txt b/collection-lib/CMakeLists.txt
index e1e19cd..4ff5c5a 100644
--- a/collection-lib/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/collection-lib/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -28,6 +28,13 @@ add_library(collection_lib STATIC
 # reason in a non-PIC object).
 set_target_properties(collection_lib PROPERTIES POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE ON)
 
+# aleks2 (H38): a switch-arm64 module may not use thread-local storage (the loader has no TLS blocks, and no
+# TLS support is planned). The only TLS in this library is stb_image's failure reason, so it is built without it.
+# tex_replacements.cpp says why that is safe (stb_image has one single-threaded user).
+if (DUSK_SWITCH_ARM64_MODULE_TOOLCHAIN)
+    target_compile_definitions(collection_lib PRIVATE STBI_NO_THREAD_LOCALS)
+endif ()
+
 target_include_directories(collection_lib PUBLIC ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include)
 # dusklight_mod_api: SDK service headers. dusklight_game_abi_headers: the game's
 # public include dirs + compile definitions. Deliberately NOT
diff --git a/collection-lib/src/tex_replacements.cpp b/collection-lib/src/tex_replacements.cpp
index effd324..a250f07 100644
--- a/collection-lib/src/tex_replacements.cpp
+++ b/collection-lib/src/tex_replacements.cpp
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <atomic>
 #include <cmath>
 #include <cstdarg>
 #include <cstdio>
@@ -8,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <fstream>
 #include <new>
 #include <string>
+#include <thread>
 #include <vector>
 
 #include <mods/svc/host.h>
@@ -185,10 +187,28 @@ static ResTIMG* tex_rep_build_override(ResTIMG* original, const u8* pngPixels, i
     return reinterpret_cast<ResTIMG*>(buffer);
 }
 
+// aleks2 (H38): on the console this library is built with STBI_NO_THREAD_LOCALS -- the module loader provides no TLS
+// block, and stb_image's failure reason is thread-local unless told otherwise -- so stbi_failure_reason() is one
+// global here. That is safe only while stb_image has a single, single-threaded user: tex_replacements_apply() is
+// its only caller in this library and in the mod, and it runs on the game thread (load_icon_uncached, a game-thread
+// load of the Collection screen's icons; neither the library nor the mod starts a thread). The first caller is taken
+// as that thread and a call from any other is refused instead of racing on the decoder's state.
+static std::atomic<std::thread::id> g_texRepOwner{};
+
+static bool tex_rep_on_owner_thread() {
+    std::thread::id owner{};
+    const std::thread::id me = std::this_thread::get_id();
+    return g_texRepOwner.compare_exchange_strong(owner, me) || owner == me;
+}
+
 ResTIMG* tex_replacements_apply(const char* resPath, ResTIMG* fallback) {
     if (fallback == nullptr) {
         return nullptr;
     }
+    if (!tex_rep_on_owner_thread()) {
+        tex_rep_log("texture replacement '%s': called off the game thread, not decoded", resPath);
+        return fallback;
+    }
 
     std::filesystem::path pngPath;
     std::error_code ec;
